So, are you enjoying my company?

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.720
Yeah. You don't bother me by
talking my ear off, like other girls do.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.590
You're also elegant and beautiful.
You make wonderful company.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:47.890
Y-Yes, chatterboxes are
quite unpleasant, aren't they?

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:57.030
Eek!
The Boy in the Manor
is a Terminator

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.800
Hey, move it.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.810
Those two sure are laid-back.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.780
The case still hasn't been solved,
yet they've gone and taken a long vacation.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.980
Well, those girls are human, too.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:09.620
Even they need a break sometime.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.480
Ah, hot!

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.660
Anyway, Chief...
These sure look real, don't they?

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:16.120
Give me back my money!

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.190
That's the counterfeit.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.600
You seem to understand
those girls pretty well.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.700
However, this is no ordinary case.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.000
The counterfeit money in circulation
is causing is an economic crisis.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.310
One bank in particular has taken a direct hit,
and is about to go bankrupt.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.240
Now is no time for a vacation!

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:32.670
Just assign someone else to the case.
Now is no time for a vacation!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.580
Just assign someone else to the case.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.670
These days, being too strict
will only push younger people away.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.410
Gooley here.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.550
What? You found Jobs Garou's hideout?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.030
Tamul Island?

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:50.330
That's right. I want you to leave immediately.
Tamul Island?

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.830
That's right. I want you to leave immediately.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.290
Immediately?

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.800
You've had enough time off, haven't you?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.100
Hm? Where's Yuri?

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.200
She's out enjoying her youth.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.730
What are you getting at?

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.610
Youth doesn't come twice.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.940
Yuri's just like any other girl
when she's off work.

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.240
Is that so?

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.540
I'll do it alone this time.
It's a pretty easy job, right?

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.480
It seems you have a beautiful friendship.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:17.320
Fine, but doing this job
alone could be dangerous.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.880
I'll get a guy who understands
you very well to help.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.520
Is he a hunk?

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.130
Sure, I guess.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.220
Now go.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.450
Looks like I might get to
enjoy my youth, too!

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:54.590
I'll be leaving now!

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:55.120
Wait!
I'll be leaving now!

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:55.590
Wait!

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.690
You're late. I almost froze.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:02.500
What do you want?
What are you doing here?

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.200
Chief's orders. I'm here to
join you on your mission.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.170
Ehh?!

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.940
So the "Trouble Consultant
who understands me well" is...

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.170
Yours truly.
So the "Trouble Consultant
who understands me well" is...

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:08.900
Yours truly.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:16.140
So, are you impressed? I graduated with top
marks from the 3WA training school, you know.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.080
But you have zero experience in the field...

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.810
What a headache.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.730
The heroine in that book
must be an amazing woman.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:36.290
Yes. She's my ideal goddess,
my beautiful Madonna...

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:49.200
Uh, Y-Yuri?

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.680
What is it?

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.480
Don't mind me, just keep reading your book!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:57.470
Uh, d-don't you t-think it's a bit
dangerous to speed like this at night?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.120
Oh my, not at all!
I usually drive much faster.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.280
I-I see...

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.830
It's already winter around here, isn't it?

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:11.600
We'll be arriving at Garou's island soon.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.030
I don't get it, though.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:16.570
Why would a top electronic engineer
get involved with printing counterfeit money?

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:21.540
The guy's 60 years old. Don't you think the guns
are a bit much? This isn't the Normandy landing.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:26.650
Nope! A great Tro Con must always
be fully equipped and prepared.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:30.350
I just hope all of this doesn't turn
the docile goat into a fearsome tiger.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.350
I'm home.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.730
Guess Kei's a little bitter, huh?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.470
Kei, I brought you a present.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.040
It's Mush House's...

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.330
Sorry to keep you waiting, Mack.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.990
Why don't we have some tea?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:54.300
We have guests.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.630
It's not often we get visitors on this island.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:05.110
That building on the summit is Garou's manor.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.770
His counterfeit-money factory
is in the basement.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.280
How do you know?

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.550
Because counterfeit-money factories
are always in the basement.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:18.790
Well. I see they've brought
all sorts of violent gifts for us.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:20.560
What should we do, dear?

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:24.070
It's quite bothersome to be
cordial to strangers at my age.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.860
I'm sure if I just scare
them a little, they'll leave.

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:33.630
Jeez...

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.050
W-What is that?!

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:41.780
My master does not welcome you.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.340
Please leave.

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.950
It's just a messenger robot.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.550
Don't scare us like that!
We're from the 3WA.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.820
We've come here for the
main suspect in the counterfeit m-

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:57.160
Seems it'll take more than
childish tricks to scare off the 3WA.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.400
Your tea is getting cold, dear.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:08:59.730
Ah.
Your tea is getting cold, dear.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.970
Eh?!

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.870
Kei went by herself?

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.510
Yes, while you were out
enjoying your so-called "youth."

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:07.810
She's probably at Tamul Island by now.

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.450
Oh Kei, trying to be thoughtful.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.010
I want you to head there immediately.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.350
I sent Calico to help her,
but I still have my doubts.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:15.480
Calico?!

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.490
Y-Yeah, that is rather worrisome.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:18.350
I'll leave right away.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:18.620
Hold on.
I'll leave right away.

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.650
Hold on.

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:22.850
I've just received some new
information about Jobs Garou.

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.330
Apparently he had a son.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.600
A son?

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:32.830
But the son committed suicide six years ago.
His name was Mack Garou, he was 27 at the time.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.700
He worked at a bank, but he got dragged into
the upper management's illegal activities...

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.540
...and ended up as their scapegoat.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.680
It's a familiar tale.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.550
That was probably the reason for his suicide.

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:48.080
Jobs Garou printed counterfeit money and
caused this crisis to avenge his son, didn't he?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.020
Most likely. Now, hurry.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:50.920
Aye-aye, sir!

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.450
What do you think you're doing?

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:04.830
I just saved you from
a dangerous enemy mech.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.440
That wasn't a combat mech.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:09.500
You can never be too careful!

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.510
Firing without confirming
the target. That's one demerit!

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.000
Why you little...

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.880
What happened to "confirming the enemy"?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:23.910
Take a good look.
It has a built-in beam gun.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:28.020
Lacking the ability to make quick decisions.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.280
That's two demerits.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.060
Sounds like it's started.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:37.530
Please, nothing too violent, dear.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.760
Don't worry, I'll just knock
them out. I won't kill them.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.960
Okay, how about this?

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.440
Oh, you got me.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.610
I'll go first, so back me up, okay?

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:51.780
Jeez.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:55.640
Calico!

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:13.020
What are you doing?

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.680
This is the same as being
attacked from both sides!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.450
Calico, stop shooting!

00:11:57.310 --> 00:11:57.870
Kei!

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.200
You fat, ugly, flat-nosed, *censored*!

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:29.370
If she was okay, she would have
responded with something ten times worse.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.070
Kei, you've messed up.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.760
She's awake.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:49.300
This wouldn't have happened
if you had just left quietly.

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:51.420
You're Mylene and Jobs Garou, aren't you?

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.030
Calico!

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.000
Where am I?

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:02.940
I'm sorry for putting you in
such an uncomfortable position.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.280
Jobs Garou!

00:13:05.280 --> 00:13:07.410
You're under arrest for counterfei-ahh!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:10.820
My, such an angry reaction.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.950
All we wanted...

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:15.990
...was to get back at that
bank for framing our son.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:19.630
Save it for the judge... Dammit!

00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:23.300
Thanks to you two, Eleanor City has
fallen into an economic crisis.

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.870
That wasn't our intention.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.600
I said, save it for the-!

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:34.440
"Our beloved son, Mack Garou..."

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:36.680
"...rests here."

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.110
I wonder where Kei's resting?

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.640
The dead silence bothers me.

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:48.450
We've avenged our son.

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:55.750
We no longer have any need for these.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.170
That was the last one.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:07.580
We will never again make counterfeit money.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:12.880
If you had just left us alone, we
could have lived out our lives in peace.

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.780
Whatever your reasons,
what you did is a crime.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:21.520
We know.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:26.160
We'll leave here and go
somewhere quiet, out of sight.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:29.720
Though it pains us to leave this island,
which Mack loved so much.

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:51.050
I will start preparing dinner.
What would you like?

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.450
Ah, um... Let's see...

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:59.360
I'd like a Lyonnaise salmon pie,
chicken terrine, and an ecrevisse salad.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.830
Certainly.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.210
Ah, while you're at it,
I'd like some consommé, too.

00:15:13.210 --> 00:15:14.400
Certainly.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:45.610
M-Mack?

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:47.310
B-But you're supposed to be dead...

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:49.900
Ahhh, a ghost!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.180
W-What?

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:56.250
Kei's the one who likes horror movies.
She asks me to watch them with her,

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:58.520
but then I can't go to the
bathroom by myself afterwards...

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:02.750
A-A-Anyway, I hate soy pulp (okara)
And I hate the occult! (okaruto)

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.590
Stay away!

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.230
What could that be?

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:14.100
Yuri?

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:19.500
How tasteless, making a robot
that looks just like his son.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:22.740
I'll go check it out.

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:26.300
Okay now, I need you to
be quiet for a while.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:28.480
You'd best stay quiet, too.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:33.280
If you make any loud noises, you'll trigger the
automatic sensor and turn on the laser beam.

00:16:33.920 --> 00:16:36.750
You say such scary things
with such a gentle face...

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:41.560
The basement, huh?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:02.610
You're a pretty tough guy.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:06.420
Mack!

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:09.350
Dear!

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:13.820
Mack, what's wrong?
Stop being so violent!

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.130
What are they doing upstairs?

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.230
Keep it down!

00:17:23.340 --> 00:17:24.800
Stop, Mack!

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:26.100
Please, don't!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:30.100
Dear...

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.510
The override system has been...

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.180
C'mon, now!

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.260
Shoot his neck!

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:43.820
That's where all the central
circuits are gathered!

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:44.090
He's no longer...
That's where all the central
circuits are gathered!

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.220
He's no longer...

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:48.800
Sounds like a real ruckus up there.

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:50.890
It just has to be Yuri.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:54.370
Hey, you! Stop goofing off
and come help me!

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.230
That's easier said than done!

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.190
All right!

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.870
Wait, where are you going?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:03.640
Well...

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:04.250
...it's not...

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:04.850
...going where I...

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:05.780
...want it to!

00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.320
You idiot! What have you done?!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.050
Yuri! Yuri!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:22.050
Damn.

00:18:23.970 --> 00:18:25.130
Let's get to the basement.

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.810
Game over.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.180
Yuri!

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.910
Calico!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:47.020
Yuri! If you're gonna
help me, then hurry up!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.050
I won't be able to get married!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.020
Y-Yuri!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.590
Yuri, over here!

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:57.800
Oh, Kei. You okay?

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.030
No, I'm not! This thing's
gonna split me in half!

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:01.830
Hurry up and stop it!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.100
